{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/31636-non-ww-rpgs-we-play-and-love","id":31636,"title":"Non-WW RPGs we play and love","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-17T07:08:30-08:00","id":31636,"title":"Non-WW RPGs we play and love","content":"Apologies if there's a similar thread somewhere; I couldn't find it.<br /> <br /> This is sort of what I expected from the &quot;Games Discussion&quot; thread; I've contributed there, too, but I'm curious as to what other tabletop RPGs people play around here.<br /> <br /> I'm a big, huge TSR-era D&amp;D nerd. I like 3e and 4e well enough, as a player anyway (playing a 3.5e/d20 L5R game right now), but it's TSR-era stuff and its OSR derivatives that really get me going. Of the original crop, I favor the <b>D&amp;D Rules Cyclopedia</b>; on the OSR front I am a big, huge fan of <b>Adventurer Conqueror King System (ACKS)</b>, which pretty much feels like the D&amp;D RC capped at level 14 and honed to a razor-fine edge, and of <b>Astonishing Swordsmen &amp; Sorcerers of Hyperborea (AS&amp;SH)</b>, which feels like AD&amp;D 1e or OD&amp;D by way of Weird Tales pulps and Tales From The Crypt comics. But right now I'm running <b>Swords &amp; Wizardry Complete </b>for a classic, OD&amp;D-powered, super-deadly dungeon-crawling romp.<br /> <br /> I am absolutely, head over heels in love with <b>Runequest 6th edition</b>. In a review elsewhere, I called it &quot;the Cadillac of Runequests&quot; and I stand by that assesment. It's become my go-to game for non-D&amp;D fantasy. I can run pretty much any fantasy setting I know or imagine with this hefty but clear tome of goodness.<br /> <br /> <b>Call of Cthulhu</b> is a classic, I know. I've used it to run Mythos and non-Mythos horror scenarios to great effect. I've done subdued investigative games and pulpy shoot-cultist-in-the-face cheap thrill romps. I love it that the game supports both.<br /> <br /> <b>Mongoose Traveller</b> is a game I am very much new to, and I ran it only once, and I'd love to revisit it. I love the &quot;gambling&quot; feel of character generation.<br /> <br /> <b>Savage Worlds</b> was my go-to system for a while, and I'm a bit burned out on it, but my players have been begging for a return of my wildly successful <b>Day After Ragnarok</b> campaign. I've been pondering whether to do it with the &quot;gritty combat&quot; option from the new SW Deluxe, or whether to try something else (I know there's a FATE version around, but I'm not much of a FATE fan).<br /> <br /> <b>Wild Talents</b> I've been meaning to try for a while now. I have yet to find a supers system that I love and I suspect WT might be the one.<br /> <br /> <b>Eclipse Phase</b> I've also yet to play. I had little contact with transhuman SF before buying it and it got me reading a few of the classics; I should really find the time to run it. Maybe as a radically different follow-up to my current D&amp;D dungeon slog.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, I'm a huge fan of <b>Palladium</b> RPGs in general and <b>Rifts</b> in particular. I find that the system generally isn't as bad as the Internet would have it, just abysmally presented. A few charts (like they used in the old Palladium Fantasy RPG 1e) would go a long, long way towards making the game easier to run and play, as well as cleaning up a few contradictory rulings (e.g. attacks per round, burst fire). I've tried conversions in that past but really, nothing beats having a dragon and a hobo in the same adventuring party, with the hobo roleplaying circles around the dragon by dint of a clever and glib player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1714-the-butcher","name":"The Butcher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T07:53:34-08:00","id":31667,"title":"","content":"Earthdawn. I frickin' love Earthdawn. If I was trapped on a deserted island with five people, dice, and only one book, it would be Earthdawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T08:16:37-08:00","id":31680,"title":"","content":"Cyberpunk 2020. I still carry the 10 sided I played it with in my pocket as a good luck charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T15:59:19-08:00","id":31960,"title":"","content":"<b>GURPS</b> is my preferred system. I use various editions of D&amp;D (mainly 3.5 and 4 these days), because the systems are still a distinct part of player expectations, no matter how broken they can be. Often <i>because</i> of how broken they can be. And I run a heavily house-ruled version of the default system for Exalted, because I'm too lazy to translate it over. But everything else I run in GURPS. Old and New World of Darkness, In Nomine, Shadowrun, Earthdawn, Marvel Superheroes, Star Wars, and a dozen other over the years, I find it much easier to translate them all into GURPS than to learn each proprietary system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","user":"The Hanged Man","date":". 12-17-2013, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T16:36:16-08:00","id":31985,"title":"","content":"Fourth Edition D&amp;D is my number one non-WW RPG. It wasn't the first edition I played, but it was the first I could call my own, and I especially enjoyed how the system of powers was set up. <br /> <br /> My only wish is that somebody had licensed its use for a CRPG, because it's <i>so perfectly set up</i> for that. Every class and every monster operates using the same basic system of powers. Under that framework, even the most exotic material (ex. psionics) could be implemented without much difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T16:53:17-08:00","id":32000,"title":"","content":"I'm Devouring Chuubo, and really want to give it a try once I'm in less dire straits, and through that Nobilis! Love me some Moran!<br /> <br /> I want to look into Saturday Morning Adventures cause that sounds like simple fun fun! Savage Worlds has caught my interest through praise by various other writers in the industry. And I want to eventually look into Zeitgeist cause I like the idea of a game built to model a sci fi movie with simple rules, and then Amarathine since well see how its handled. And Curse the Darkness is free right? I want to give that a read when I can.<br /> <br /> Oh and some sort of Marvel RPG. I'm a Marvel fan after all, and Whitewolf actually is what stole my resources from hemorrhaging into Marvel. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T17:06:59-08:00","id":32013,"title":"","content":"My favorites are Dark Heresy and the other 40k RPGs and D&amp;D4E. WHFRP2E is really solid as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T17:14:55-08:00","id":32016,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu, D&amp;D...MMORPG is Runescape (Elisabeth does WoW, but she hooked me on RS).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T21:11:58-08:00","id":32139,"title":"","content":"I like the Warhammer 40k universe a lot, as well as the respective games. Unfortunately, I'm not a huge fan of the system. Too many charts! When I run Warhammer 40k games, I tend to just toss out the system and use something else. <br /> <br /> I used to be a big Palladium fan, and while I'm not one anymore, there are still a few games that I enjoyed like Nightbane. I also ended up as a fan of CJ Carella; his stuff like WitchCraft was pretty darn good. Shame he has largely dropped out of the RPG community, though chatting with him, he's made tentative suggestions he might be dropping back in with a new project at some point.<br /> <br /> Nobilis is amazing. I haven't had the chance to ever play it, but I love the conceptual space. <br /> <br /> Other than that, while I've played lots and lots of systems over the decades, those are the only games (other than White Wolf ones) that have really stood out to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T21:59:44-08:00","id":32160,"title":"","content":"I've had lots of fun with some of the more freeform indie games, in particular Fiasco. I can Fiasco day after day, and it's different each time.<br /> <br /> Ars Magica is pretty cool. Although it's not White Wolf, Mark Rein-Hagan was co-creator on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T05:20:35-08:00","id":37277,"title":"","content":"I always was a fan of D&amp;D, Pathfinder, and Big Eyes Small Mouth. Currently working on a conversion of Classic World of Darkness to BESM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T07:33:47-08:00","id":37316,"title":"","content":"I'm in a game using the Pathfinder system to run the 3.0 setting Dragonstar (Sci-fi D&amp;D in SPAAAAACE). I'd love to give Chuubo's a chance, and I've got Houses of the Blooded and I'd love to be in a game of that which went properly (my wife was soured on it by the first game we were in spending half the session going through several &quot;seasons&quot; and thus spending a LOT of time on resource management.)<br /> <br /> Also, Don't Rest Your Head. I've got it, but I'm just a little worried that I don't have my head fully wrapped around it's nightmarish Dark-City-Meets-Phantom-Tollbooth aesthetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:11:12-08:00","id":37326,"title":"","content":"Not enough time in the world to list them all, but how 'bout a few highlights?<br /> <br /> My girlfriend (and fellow Onyx Path freelancer), Monica Valentinelli, is the brand manager for the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?cPath=331_10283&amp;affiliate_id=22713&amp;src=MMMWW\" target=\"_blank\">Firefly RPG</a> from Margaret Weis Productions. So, we've been playtesting that quite a bit and having a blast.<br /> <br /> I'm really digging the *Word system lately and poking at a campaign setting for <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/108028?affiliate_id=22713&amp;src=MMMWW\" target=\"_blank\">Dungeon World</a>, that I hope to publish late 2014.<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T11:34:32-08:00","id":37422,"title":"","content":"I love the Dresden Files RPG, as well as FATE. If I ever run another game, I will probably use the FATE System instead of any other. It's fast and fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T11:51:13-08:00","id":37430,"title":"","content":"I started roleplaying on Dungeons and Dragons (3.0 to 3.5) but when I came to university I absolutely fell in love with White Wolf games in particular World of Darkness. However, despite all its issues DnD has remained something of a favourite for me and I still play it semi-regularly. Though I've tried 4th Edition and while it was enjoyable I wasn't particularly sold on it over all, I have in the last few months got reading the various pathfinder supplements and absolutely adore what they've done with archetypes and the additional classes (I love Gunslinger and Alchemist in particular). I'm also a big fan of the Iron Kingdoms setting (and Warmachine of course) but I've not got a chance to try out or look at in any depth their new roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> In the last 18 months I was exposed to and have run Eclipse Phase, which is another absolutely beautiful game that changed my opinion on percentile systems. Its one that I have every intention of running for a longer period of time in future given that I actually managed to freak my players out last time (huzzah).<br /> I'm also a big fan of Mutants and Masterminds by Green Ronin and am still playing the second edition, my only issue is character generation is a chore and its hard to keep games from becoming completely and absolutely rediculous which often ruins my intention of running the grittier and more serious side. I've taken a break from running the game for anything more than one shots, its still one of my favourite systems and proves infinietly enjoyable so long as players stick to their concepts/themes. I'm also intending to run alongside a friend of mine a Dragonage game but I need to look at the system more.<br /> I recently began playing L5R (4th ed) which so far I'm loving for the game itself, the interesting mechanics and the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T17:41:59-08:00","id":37577,"title":"","content":"Before xmas I played a really cool season of monsterhearts and I'm going to try lords of gossamer and shadow soon. I really like the Apocalypse World engine and I guess it's pretty cool that eclipse phase is getting a fate mod because the setting's sure interesting but I really hate percentile systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T12:40:22-08:00","id":37961,"title":"","content":"Let's see...<br /> <br /> AD&amp;D 2nd Edition (that's where I started being a gamer, so it is a special game fore me).<br /> Rules Cylcopedia or BECM D&amp;D and this D&amp;D &quot;next&quot; are currently battling it out in my brain for the title of Current Favorite D&amp;D.<br /> I also play Pathfinder quite a lot and don't completely hate it.<br /> <br /> Call of Cthulhu, Savage Worlds, Aces &amp; Eights, HackMaster, TSR Marvel Super Heroes and the Lord of the Rings coda system all have a place on my post-unused-game-book-purge book shelf.<br /> <br /> The one I really have to mention though, is Shadowrun - I don't play it nearly as much as I'd like to, but I keep two editions of it (3rd and 5th) on hand because it is the only game which I have played, will play again, and have never once thought &quot;I think I might just be done with this game&quot; which I have thought about everything else I've ever played at one point or another - and even sworn off particular editions of games (no more 1st or 2nd Edition Exalted, 1st Edition Scion, D&amp;D 3.5 or 4e, for example).<br /> <br /> And then, things I have never played but would certainly like to try out... which I can only think of one of right now: Godlike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T14:58:58-08:00","id":38023,"title":"","content":"What? There are other games? Why didn't anyone tell ME!?<br /> <br /> Although I don't play it much anymore, I enjoyed 4th edition of Legend of the Five Rings while I was living in London for a short time. I tend to enjoy different things and look through some books for fun and inspiration, but don't play many of them. Ever. It saddens me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T17:11:07-08:00","id":38974,"title":"","content":"I really want to do a Chuubo Game! Like for Reals you guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T06:04:40-08:00","id":39340,"title":"","content":"Now that I found out that the Elder Scrolls may have started as a RQ campaign I'm tempted to make an Elder Scrolls game using the RQ system or the BRP (are they actually the same?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T15:37:53-08:00","id":40188,"title":"","content":"Warhammer 40k, I was so..not interested when it was suggested by my husband, but he bribed me into making a character, I did not read the book and he walked me through what to do. I was only SLIGHTLY intrigued, then we started playing, and I got more and more interested, even read the book and now over a year later i'm totally hooked.<br /> <br /> Pathfinder, for those days i'm just not wanting to role play, but still want to do something fun. My ST doesnt mind running pathfinder as a roll-play, and its the ONLY game he allows this in and its a nice breath of fresh air(especially after many exalted sessions where my ST has a strict policy on minimal rolling(except in combat, where rolling is completely needed), and active description to handle things if possible. x.x )<br /> <br /> I'm interested in Shadowrun sorta, as well as working on my own setting in hopes of convince my st to run it..I want a post apoc game, but I dont want mutants or magic, nor a HUGE timeskip(like in i think it was Gamma world? where it was far enough in the future that no one remember what even basic tech was.)<br /> <br /> We've also played a few custom games using various systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:50:28-08:00","id":41137,"title":"","content":"Does BESM count as a non-White Wolf game anymore? Last I checked WW bought those rights, and is basically just using them as an excuse to sell PDFs of the old books. Anyway, I play BESM, Anima: Beyond Fantasy, Mekton Z, and that about covers the systems I've played and liked for system and setting (when applicable and is not a White Wolf/Onyx Path creation). There are a few I think have interesting settings, but I really prefer not touching with a 20 foot pole (Rifts, Robotech, Babylon 5 and Star Wars), or have a system that looks interesting but without putting a lot of effort to divorce it from its setting I'm never going to try it (Warhammer 40K, though supposedly the new Star Wars games use the same basic concept of a system).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T09:54:48-08:00","id":41166,"title":"","content":"I think I own every Rifts book out there. Not to play, but to read. Siembeda and his crew write damn well. Add to some incredible artwork;<br /> <img src=\"https://palladium-store.com/mm5/graphics/00000002/images/PR804-Rare-1996-Print-Rifts-Juicer-Uprising.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://thumbs2.ebaystatic.com/d/l225/m/mPi-aOnhyG9GtzDOV57FMqQ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <a href=\"http://img508.imageshack.us/img508/2324/riftstolkeenblazingironrn7.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Blazing Iron Juggernaut</a><br /> <br /> irresistible..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T10:18:27-08:00","id":41183,"title":"","content":"Lets see.<br /> <br /> 40k (Only War is frigging awesome), Dnd (2nd and 3.5), Iron Kingdoms (3.5, haven't tried the lates edition yet), Palladium (Rifts, playing just barely, can't get the group together), Pirates of the Spanish Main (Savage World), d20 Future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T02:47:36-08:00","id":41594,"title":"","content":"well AD&amp;D got me hooked on rpgs, and i still have a huge soft spot for the old forgotten realms and ravenloft settings. i have tried GURPS (didnt really care for it), pathfinder, Warhammer 40k (love the setting, hate the rules), warhammer fantasy (samething as 40k). and lately i tried getting in to trail of chutulu and savage worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21-draven","name":"Draven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:50:01-08:00","id":44579,"title":"","content":"Sundered Skies, Rogue Trader, Shadowrun 4th and Warhammer Fantasy RPG ... ah, the luxury of still being in college.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1854-ser-arthur-dayne","name":"Ser Arthur Dayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:10:22-08:00","id":81717,"title":"","content":"I know it's an old topic, but it's still on the first page, so I'm posting in it.<br /> <br /> Has anyone had any experience with Edge of the Empire? (Age of Rebellion would work too, but I think that's still in beta.) I've been wavering back and forth on whether to pick up a copy. The dice system intrigues me, and I do like Star Wars...but on the other hand, I've heard mixed things about how it handles Force-sensitive characters, and I've been burned by FF products before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T14:27:02-08:00","id":81771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/31636-non-ww-rpgs-we-play-and-love?p=81717#post81717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's an old topic, but it's still on the first page, so I'm posting in it.<br /> <br /> Has anyone had any experience with Edge of the Empire? (Age of Rebellion would work too, but I think that's still in beta.) I've been wavering back and forth on whether to pick up a copy. The dice system intrigues me, and I do like Star Wars...but on the other hand, I've heard mixed things about how it handles Force-sensitive characters, and I've been burned by FF products before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Straight up, I have not played it, but I did read through the book repeatedly and sketch out details.<br /> <br /> While I can admit to the dice mechanic being interesting, the high price for the dice combined with charging a fairly hefty feel for a dice roller app renders me disinclined to want to support it. Also not so much a fan of the way force powers are handled since it's a very linear tree shape. You pick an effect or effects and can keep buying upgrades/boosts to it. Fine if you're spreading out so you've got a bit of mind tricking, some lightsaber skills, maybe some 'leet athletics and a bit of an ability to move stuff with your mind. Or you can just keep dumping XP into one focus and being insane at it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T15:34:44-08:00","id":81789,"title":"","content":"Not to disparage a game company, but FFG excels at finding ways to relieve you of your funds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Granted, the end result is usually a high quality product and a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> I resisted buying EotE for that very reason, the cost, until last week. I had some store credit at my FLGS, so I used it to defer some of the cost. So far, I am still digging through the crunch, but I am very impressed with the system.<br /> <br /> If you are on the fence, I suggest you check out the Edge of the Empire Beginner Game. It has the basic rules, pregens, adventure material, and a set of dice. Amazon has it listed for $23.95. The set has everything you need to play a few sessions.<br /> <br /> If you can find them, there are also sticker sheets out there to convert normal dice into EotE dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T15:49:00-08:00","id":81793,"title":"","content":"What, like a total list of games we have?<br /> <br /> Well, okay then. *Deep breath*<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dungeons and Dragons 3rd Edition<br /> Dungeons and Dragons 4th Edition<br /> Shadowrun<br /> BESM<br /> Scion<br /> A Tragedy in Five Acts<br /> Curse the Darkness<br /> Black Rock Universe<br /> Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine<br /> Cat<br /> Dresden Files<br /> Don't Rest Your Head<br /> Farewell To Fear<br /> Engine Heart<br /> Exalted Second Edition<br /> First Fable<br /> Golden Sky Stories<br /> Magicians RPG<br /> Maid RPG<br /> Mouse Guard<br /> OVA<br /> Roleplaying is Magic<br /> The Princess Game<br /> Wushu<br /> Action Planet<br /> BASH! Ultimate Edition<br /> Argyle &amp; Crew: Adventures in the Land of Skcos<br /> KidWorld<br /> Explore Beta<br /> Super Heroes Unite<br /> Teenagers from Outer Space<br /> The Play's The Thing<br /> Beyond Otaku<br /> Magical Burst(+ReWrite)<br /> Dogs In The Vineyard<br /> Spears of the Dawn<br /> Nobilis<br /> CthulhuTech<br /> Call of Cthulhu<br /> Apotheosis Drive X<br /> Witch Quest<br /> Motobushido<br /> Little Fears<br /> Puppies &amp; Pawprints<br /> Kawaii RPG's<br /> Nechronica<br /> Ryuutama<br /> Make You Kingdom<br /> The Strange<br /> <br /> ...And that might be missing a few</div></div> </div> </div><br /> The games I really want to play are, in order: 9) The Princess Game, 8) Maid RPG, 7) Beyond Otaku Dreams, 6) Black Rock Universe, 5) CthulhuTech, 4) Magicians RPG, 3) Mouse Guard, 2) Don't Rest Your Head, and 1) Golden Sky Stories.<br /> <br /> Yes. Out of that entire list of games I own, the one I want to play the most is where you play as cute little shape changing animals with small magic powers going around helping people out and making friends.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's the short of it today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T05:43:42-08:00","id":82063,"title":"","content":"My group and I are trying to convince my girlfriend to actually run a game. She seemed interested in Mouse Guard, will see how things go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:48:13-08:00","id":83737,"title":"","content":"I went ahead and ordered a copy of Edge of the Empire, and I should have it in my hands within a couple days.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping I'll get some decent use out of it, because from the free starter adventures I read online and such, it does seem like an interesting system. And as a Star Wars game, there's some pre-existing investment into the setting, even if many players - and myself, for that matter - find Force users to be the more intriguing part. (Sadly, FF's book centered around Force users won't be out until 2015.) I'll post my impressions once I've taken a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:58:29-08:00","id":83740,"title":"","content":"Does anyone here play <b>Legend of the Five Rings</b>; the RPG rather than the CCG? I kind of want to go buy some supplements (I will admit this desire is related to the sale going on at Drivethru RPG), but the only one I've purchased for the new edition, <b>Emerald Empire</b>, left a bad taste in my mouth on the grounds that it has a lot of information but no inspiration and, as such, I can't use much of it. The book doesn't seem at all concerned with giving either players or GMs ideas, instead reciting dry facts about the world like there's going to be a test on it later. I'd love to know what people think about the books released for fourth edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T03:16:34-08:00","id":83891,"title":"","content":"I own both the Core and Enemies of the Empire (basically an antagonists/bestiary book). Some of the entries in the later does have some suggestions for plot hooks (though not clearly stated as such), but it is true those books tend to be akin to fictional history books in how they read. Nevertheless, I find the setting quite interesting (as did my players) but I did have problems comming up with stories of my own for it, it seems like I'm too bound to canon and such, and can't bring myself to experiment with the setting for fear of spoiling it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T07:37:56-08:00","id":83939,"title":"","content":"I just ran across this thing... I have no idea if it's an intention spoof or just... let me assume it's intentional. I'm thinking of giving it a try in the near future because who doesn't love running space ranger bunnies, Aliens (as in from the movie) and living rock people against the evil human empire that reads exactly like a cross between warhammer 40k and the scarlet empress?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/vampire-ships-bunny-commandos-and-space-marines-lets-read-strike-legion.196770/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/data/svg/12/1/1794175159/sb_2022_favicon_192x192.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/vampire-ships-bunny-commandos-and-space-marines-lets-read-strike-legion.196770/\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire Ships, Bunny Commandos, and Space Marines: Let's Read Strike Legion </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/vampire-ships-bunny-commandos-and-space-marines-lets-read-strike-legion.196770/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/vampire-ships-bunny-commandos-and-space-marines-lets-read-strike-legion.196770/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> What do these three pictures have in common: If you answered \"they all exist in an obscure recently-released indie RPG called Strike Legion\", you're totally right. Released literally a week ago, Strike Legion, well, let's refer to the blurb. Hmm, this sounds completely original. There... </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:48:26-08:00","id":84086,"title":"","content":"My favorite RPGs outside of White Wolf games are:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www222.pair.com/sjohn/risus.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Risus: The Anything RPG</a><br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.dungeonslayers.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Dungeonslayers</a><br /> <br /> Best thing about the two games? They are free!! Head over and download them. Plus, I've made various sheets for both games. But, I love them and they're very simple systems. Risus can be used for just about anything, and Dungeonslayers is an old school dungeoncrawl game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T13:36:35-08:00","id":84195,"title":"","content":"After 40 years I have way too many RPGs in my eight bookshelves (and numerous boxes) to list, but one's that I do miss playing on a regular basis are...<br /> <br /> <b>Tri-Stat (BESM): </b>I just love this game. The ability to simulate any genre and play any character is a plus, along with the relative simplicity <i>(And yes, I know there are many other &quot;Generic&quot; RPGs -- GURPS, Hero System, etc. I have many of them...but I like Tri-Stat (BESM) the most. Sadly, I don't get to play it as much as I want to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Morrow Project: </b> A lot of fond memories, and not many games actually list you're characters Blood Type on the characters sheet, along with making it an integral part of the game. Rads are also a key part of the game too. Saving the world one person at a time.<br /> <br /> <b>Star Frontiers:</b> I loved the Dralasites, and the setting was pretty cool. Deadly as all get out, but fun.<br /> <br /> <b>Star Wars</b> (d6/West Ends): Larger than life, vast stories, bigger than life characters and plain fun.<br /> <br /> <b>Stormbringer</b> (By Chaosism): The idea of playing in the world of Michael Moorcock, with the sheer epic nature...well, it's always been appealing to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for more &quot;modern&quot; RPGs...<br /> <br /> <b>Anime Beyond Fantasy:</b> The game itself looks intriguing and it seems like it could be a very good game. I haven't had a chance to run it yet, and I'd like to give it a try in order to see how it works as opposed to just reading through it.<br /> <br /> <b>CthulhuTech:</b> The world looks very intriguing, it has a pretty gripping story with the fate of mankind hanging in the balance, and the <i>&quot;Things Man Was Not Meant To Know&quot;</i> are on the loose -- what could possibly go wrong? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dark Heresy:</b> Purge the Unclean. What can I say, I'm a sucker for hunting down the Warp Demons and their vile worshipers! Long Live the Empire! Long Live the Undead Emperor!<br /> <br /> <b>d20 3.5:</b> I tend to run this as a straight Fantasy game, and I usually put a limit on the Feats that I allow <i>(There are way too many IMO, and, if a GM is not careful, some of the 3rd party ones can unbalance a game)</i>. I like the way the rules work <i>(Mostly...I have to tweak things here and there -- especially magic...)</i>, it's pretty easy to set up a world and get things going. There is a broad spectrum of quality, but with d20 3.5 I tend to make my own world anyway -- cribbing something from one of my old campaigns long ago. <br /> <br /> <br /> There are other RPGs I play outside of WW ones. Most of them are good, and each of them have their positives and negatives -- as all things do. The main things I look for in an RPG are <i>(No particular order here...)</i>:<br /> <br /> 1) The Rules should not get in the way of the Groups fun.<br /> 2) The Setting should not get in the way of the Groups fun.<br /> 3) Consistency should be maintained throughout the book(s), both in relation to the Rules and the Setting.<br /> <br /> As long as these three things are there, more or less, then the STs job is easier and the potential for entertainment is increased for the Group. When any of the above are an issue, then it becomes harder for the ST and group to have fun -- which is what gaming is about.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for reading. I return you to you're regularly scheduled thread.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:38:31-08:00","id":84536,"title":"","content":"So far, my favorite non-WW system is <b>Wild Talents</b>. It's incredibly flexible, very, very well-balanced, and has enough crunch to be interesting but not so much that it's overwhelming.<br /> <br /> I also like the <b>FATE</b> system for certain things, but it just doesn't strike me interesting, you know? Rather, to be particular, I find the way that it handles powers pretty boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T14:54:04-07:00","id":92476,"title":"","content":"Cybperunk 2020<br /> Deep-Space<br /> Maximum Metal - Shockwave!<br /> Night's-Edge (Grimm's Cybertales)<br /> <br /> Dungeons &amp; Dragons 1/2e (sometimes played in OWoD)<br /> Dark-Sun<br /> Red/Blue/Green boxes (low magic)<br /> <br /> Classic Battletech<br /> <br /> Babylon 5 RPG &amp; Full Thrust<br /> <br /> Palladium's Recon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T16:55:04-07:00","id":93074,"title":"","content":"Right now, we are playing mostly WW games but our group is also doing a game of Deadlands and loving it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T17:28:14-07:00","id":93088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/31636-non-ww-rpgs-we-play-and-love?p=84536#post84536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, my favorite non-WW system is <b>Wild Talents</b>. It's incredibly flexible, very, very well-balanced, and has enough crunch to be interesting but not so much that it's overwhelming.<br /> <br /> I also like the <b>FATE</b> system for certain things, but it just doesn't strike me interesting, you know? Rather, to be particular, I find the way that it handles powers pretty boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Godlike/Wild Talents has link to the WoD in the name of Greg Stolze. <br /> <br /> The games I am interested in are Cthulhu and Delta Green, some Unisystem (Witchcraft, Conspiracy X), a lot of Savage Worlds settings (Deadlands, Solomon Kane, Hellfrost, Slipstream, 50 Fanthoms, Necessary Evil), Godlike/Wild Talents, Traveller and Fading Suns. I also don't mind Warhammer (both Fantasy and 40K), Shadowrun, Spycraft and Dark Matter although I am not that fond of D20 as a system. Of all those my favorite setting is Savage Worlds Hellfrost. It's some sort of run of the mill fantasy setting, only with a spin. It's a really broad kitchen sinky type of setting with just the right amount of detail to it. Broad enough to go in all kinds of different direction, but not detailed enough to get setting lawyers to ruin the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T03:52:31-07:00","id":99905,"title":"","content":"Currently I'm playing in a lot of <b>Hero</b> System games, and enjoying them greatly. I also run an <b>Eclipse Phase</b> game and another game of my own design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T15:00:56-07:00","id":102952,"title":"","content":"Playing in a weekly DnD 3.5 game, as well as a bi-monthly DnD 4th game, and enjoying them both.<br /> Trying to get my friend to dust off his old Shadowrun books, but he is kinda leery about relearning the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}